Unicorns are a special case to the general altar conversion routine.

To convert an altar, you need:
	1) a fresh corpse
		a) this means no undead corpses need apply, they were
                    too old when they were walking.
		b) acid blob corpses are good until they vanish
	2) an altar not of your alignment (QED)
	3) the ability for your deity to hear you
		a) i.e. Valley of the Dead, Orcus' temple, and the Inner
		   Sanctum are ineligible
	4) be in good standing with your deity
		a) they *can* be angry at you, but if you are
		  'insufficiently lawful/neutral/chaotic' then
		  you may convert yourself.
	5) a unicorn corpse not of your alignment.
		a) if you sac a unicorn of your own alignment on an
		   altar of your own alignment, you tick
		   off your own deity.
		b) if you sac a unicorn of your own alignment on an
		   altar of either of the other two alignments, you
		   convert yourself (if possible).
		c) if you sac a unicorn of either of the other two on
		   your own, "you feel you are thoroughly on the right
		   path!"
	        d) if you sac a unicorn of either of the other two on
		   an altar that's aligned to them, you tick off *that*
		   *that* diety, who may send minions (angels,
		   (elementals, or demons), or other ills, the corpse
		   isn't touched, and the altar stays the same.
	 	e) with a cross aligned unicorn on an altar not aligned
		   to you or the corpse, the usual chance of converting
		   the altar.


